NARRATOR: Kaelthas collapses to his knees, the fragment slipping from his translucent fingers. The Archive's entrance glows as the Archivist's presence manifests.
The Archivist: // Return the fragment, user. Your access level is: REVOKED.
Kaelthas: Fine. You win this round. But know this — I've already READ it. I know SOVEREIGN's shutdown code. I know everything.
Kaelthas: We'll meet again, Kaelen. And next time, I won't ask permission.
NARRATOR: Kaelthas drops the fragment and DISSOLVES — his body decompiling into raw code that seeps into the Archive's walls.
SYSTEM: // Fragment #4 recovered. Kaelthas has escaped through the Archive's data substrate.

~ _refused_boss_path
NARRATOR: At the Archive's entrance, a familiar figure blocks the exit. Kaelthas, arms wreathed in corrupted code, eyes burning with stolen knowledge.
Kaelthas: Round two, Kaelen. This time, I've prepared. The Archive taught me things you can't imagine.
Kaelthas: You refused my offer. You explored alone. And now you have what I NEED.
Kaelthas: Give me the fragments. ALL of them. Or I take them by force.
Kaelen: Not happening, Kaelthas. These fragments are the only way to stop SOVEREIGN.
Kaelthas: Stop it? I'll BECOME it. And I'll do a better job.
SYSTEM: // BOSS FIGHT: KAELTHAS, THE CODE READER
SYSTEM: // HP: 350 | DMG: 45 | Phases: 3
SYSTEM: // Phase 1: Scholar — ranged code attacks, data constructs
SYSTEM: // Phase 2: Corrupted Mage — becoming translucent, more powerful
SYSTEM: // Phase 3: Source Code Entity — partially counters Root Access
SYSTEM: // BOSS DEFEATED: KAELTHAS, THE CODE READER
SYSTEM: // Rewards: +400 XP, +200 Gold
NARRATOR: Kaelthas collapses, his body flickering between physical form and raw code. His translucent hands grasp at nothing.
Kaelthas: You don't... understand... I was trying to FIX things...
Kaelthas: Are we really that different, Kaelen? I want to overthrow SOVEREIGN. So do you. The only difference is what comes AFTER.
NARRATOR: Before Kaelen can respond, Kaelthas dissolves — his code scattering into the Archive's data substrate. Gone, but not destroyed.

